**Clarifying child updates**

I’m realizing that updating a child deactivates the old one while the new one gets inflated. Inactive elements get unmounted during the finalizeTree step after building. So it seems the correct order is to initialize the new child, register it, and then dispose of the old child later. This removes the registry entry. Aha, that explains the absence of the p-convert entry! It's quite a puzzle, but I think I've got it figured out.
